					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1619822#post-2475381</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1619822/volume-19-113-a-01:of-the-instruments-composers-and-the-conf#post-2475381</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 19 Mar 2016 03:32:32 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Hercules Rockefeller</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2314402</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I really, really like this.</p> <p>The first half was fascinating - for some reason, despite my near-complete lack of familiarity with the CotBG (I haven't caught up on all the GoIs yet, leave me alone!), I had no trouble understanding the esoteric writing. I thought your descriptions of the planets were especially lovely.</p> <p>And, as others before me have noted, shifting the focus to Spline in the second half was a really neat idea, one that made me impatient to read the rest of the series.</p> <p>Easy upvote.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1619822#post-2469849</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1619822/volume-19-113-a-01:of-the-instruments-composers-and-the-conf#post-2469849</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 09 Mar 2016 03:58:01 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>sirpudding</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>348648</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>It's tough to write biblical-style ecclesiastical verse, but this works really well. I really like the shift in styles when Inventor Spline is writing. I definitely appreciate how this works to shift the Broken God from a theurgical mythical genre into science fiction, where it needs to be to work within the New Shambala storyline.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
