				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1619822/volume-19-113-a-01:of-the-instruments-composers-and-the-conf#post-2464534</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 28 Feb 2016 01:38:51 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Petrograd</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>455145</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I did enjoy it, especially the tone shift where Spline just gets down to brass tracks.</p> <p>I'm really, really unclear about Spline's logic and motivation at the end, though, and not in a cryptic or exotic way: in a purely textual way. Primary point:</p> <blockquote> <p>The point being- remote contact failed. I see no reason why direct contact wouldn't.</p> </blockquote> <p>&#8230; no reason why direct contact wouldn't&#8230; fail.</p> <p>So, double negative, every reason that it would fail. If this is the intended meaning, then I'm missing something.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
